		FV2021 Coleopteran (40 MP)
			A three-metre talk British-built humanoid combat walker used by the Canadians on Mars.  They use a new “mind-interface” neuro-helmet that makes the mecha very agile.  However, if a different pilot wants to use the mecha, the neuro-helmet must be “retuned” to their brain waves — this takes a full day; until then, halve the Defence Mastery and Combat Technique: Lightning Reflexes Attribute bonuses.  The mecha are painted standard colours: UN white, with sky-blue helmets. 
			**Derived Values**
				AR 20, HP 80
			**Mecha Sub-Attributes**
				Accessories 2 (Radio, Inertial Naviagion. 2 MP), Armour 2 (8 MP), Ground Speed 1 (Up to 50 kph. 2 MP), Life Support 2 (2 MP), Manoeuvre Bonus 4 (Ground. 4 MP), Sensors 1 (1 MP), Super-Strength 1 (3 MP), Toughness 2 (8 MP), Weapon: Plasma Fist 2 (Damage 60, Melee, Limited Shots [6 shots]. 1 MP), Weapon: Railgun 3 (Damage 45, Long-Range, Unreliable. 12 MP), Weapon: Rocket Pod 2 (Damage 45, Auto-fire, Area Effect, Limited Shots ×2 [3 shots], Stoppable. 1 MP)
			**Mecha Defects**
				Awkward Size (Huge (1-10 tonnes). 2 MBP), Hanger Queen (1 MBP), Partial Armour (1 MBP)
